Here in the Northeast, we have a full indoor track season

and that provides ample opportunity to continue to develop
our endurance athletes for the Cross Country season.

But for many Cross Country runners, offeason development
occurs during the winter.

This is an opportune time to consider developing skills
other than endurance.

http://completetrackandfield.com/winter-cross-country-training/

In this article by Complete Track & Field endurance expert
Scott Christensen, you'll get a firm understanding of where
to focus training so your Cross Country athletes continue
to improve next season.

http://completetrackandfield.com/winter-cross-country-training/

To your success,

Coach Thomas
Track & Field Association

